From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:09:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?desktop:=20right-click=20a=20gateway=20in=20the?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20device=20switcher=20=E2=86=92=20"Use=20for=20new=20sessions"?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20[daveey]?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New sessions get a sticky target separate from the gateway on screen. The device
switcher's per-row right-click saves the app-wide default route (Electron-persisted,
survives relaunch); opening a session on another gateway never changes it. ⌘N, the
command palette and the shell menu's New session now run session.new, which uses the
saved route (else 0042's This device). An unreachable saved gateway keeps the draft
bound there and offers "Create on This device instead" for that one session.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
